police in idaho say they prevented a  possible domestic terror attack over the  weekend 31 men were arrested all dressed  alike allegedly on their way to wreak  havoc at a pride event in the city of  coeur d'alene  they were found standing in the back of  a u-haul truck all had traveled from  different places and police believe they  are members of a white supremacist group  senior investigative correspondent  katherine herrich is following this for  us catherine good morning good morning  nate the fbi is assisting local police  in the investigation for now each of the  31 people arrested faces a misdemeanor  charge for conspiracy to riot law  enforcement believes the participants  are connected to a white nationalist  hate group  they came to riot downtown court  delaine's police chief said it was clear  that alleged white supremacists intended  to start a riot before they were taken  into custody near a pride celebration  saturday authorities recovered gear  including shields shin guards and a  smoke grenade these guys stopped a  u-haul full of dudes a witness tipped  off police after watching the group load  into the back of a u-haul truck at a  hotel and said they looked like a little  army they appeared to be affiliated with  the group patriot front groups that  monitor extremist ideology say patriot  front promotes fascism and the creation  of a white ethno state it was founded in  2017 after breaking off from a neo-nazi  organization that participated in the  charlottesville virginia unite the right  rally the man convicted on federal hate  crime charges for driving his car into a  crowd of protesters and killing one of  them was affiliated with that original  group they are twisting and manipulating  and misusing the idea of patriotism but  promoting a white supremacist version of  patriotism cynthia miller idris tracks  domestic extremism at american  university and told us patriot fronts  members are overwhelmingly young white  men the group arrested saturday ranged  in age from 21 to 36 and were from a  dozen different states none was local to  coeur d'alene what does the incident in  idaho tell us about the overall threat  picture we're seeing  this broadening out of the targets that  people  across this supremacist spectrum are  choosing to intimidate or harass or harm  it is part of a broader  range of anti-democratic and extremist  types of events that are happening  in this case the apparent target was  that pride event which organizers say  was the largest north idaho has ever  seen as for the 31 defendants police say  they're scheduled to be arraigned later  today they include patriot front's  alleged leader gail  all right catherine thank you very much
 

